// Syncthing ignores for the `claude` folder (~/.claude), shared Mac <-> server.
// Installed as a REAL file by claude-syncthing-ignores.nix on every host that
// shares the folder: Syncthing does not follow a symlinked .stignore, and until
// 2026-10-28 this was a nix-store symlink, so nothing below would have applied
// (credentials included). Doc: areas/second-brain/claude-sync.md.
//
// Syncthing reads top to bottom, first match wins; "!" = do NOT ignore. This is
// a whitelist: the durable Claude Code state is listed, everything else in
// ~/.claude is machine-local and stays put. On 2026-10-28 the Mac held 2.2 GB
// of fleet job state, 280 MB of security scans, digest buffers, plugin caches
// and daemon files that have no business on the server and would only conflict.

// OAuth credentials are machine-local and MUST NOT be synced. Claude Code
// rotates its refresh token on every use, so a synced token is revoked by the
// other host's next refresh: six .credentials.sync-conflict-* files and a
// "login expired" prompt several times a day, 2026-06-06 to 2026-07-11.
/.credentials.json
/.credentials.sync-conflict-*
/.syncthing..credentials.json.tmp
(?d)*.lock
(?d).DS_Store

// Synced: config, memory and conversation history (so `claude --resume`
// lists the same sessions on either host).
!/settings.json
!/settings.local.json
!/CLAUDE.md
!/keybindings.json
!/statusline-command.sh
!/agents
!/commands
!/hooks
!/skills
!/dev-mods
!/agent-memory
!/projects
!/todos
!/tasks
!/teams
!/sessions
!/plans

// Everything else is machine-local.
*
